{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/837889-2e-elements-contracts-what-can-changelings-wield","id":837889,"title":"2E Elements Contracts: What can Changelings wield?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-26T20:04:52-08:00","id":837889,"title":"2E Elements Contracts: What can Changelings wield?","content":"So, after a bit of confusion I found out on the forums that the contracts of Cloak Of The Elements and Control Elements needed to be purchased with a specific element in mind, just as the first edition of Changeling did with its own variants of the contracts. The samples that have been released have specifically noted &quot;fire, water, wind, earth, wood, metal, darkness, light and any refinement of those that make sense&quot; as being viable options for these contracts. What elements would you guys consider as other viable elements to be wielded with these contracts (and others that may emerge)?<br /> <br /> Personally, I'd advocate Sound as being one, as it is a natural and prominent force within our environment; it also doesn't hurt I have a Changeling concept who was basically used for ambient music in her Gentry's domain, and thus wielding Sound with a Cloak Of The Elements would be thematically sound (if you'd pardon the pun). Glass I'm pondering on, as it is something that Fetches and the Gentry can work their powers through, but I appreciate that it is not usually a natural occurrence. The only justification I can come up for it is if the Changeling has merged with their Fetch somehow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T20:38:55-08:00","id":837901,"title":"","content":"Teddy bears in a plush ocean.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T23:50:11-08:00","id":837962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/837889-2e-elements-contracts-what-can-changelings-wield?p=837901#post837901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Teddy bears in a plush ocean.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are surrounded by teddy bears; anyone who touches you is assaulted by their stitching and beady eyes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T01:40:10-08:00","id":837978,"title":"","content":"The thing about elements is... it's more about <i>letting</i> you do a thing than actually setting up rules for it.<br /> <br /> When these threads come up, I never quite fail to recall that line from SpellCrash where a character complains that she wasn't allowed to pick &quot;sex&quot; as her element.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T02:04:49-08:00","id":837982,"title":"","content":"Naturally, it is more or less up to the GM about what would be allowed and what would not. This is more a musings thing between the imaginations of creative individuals...and leaving open the room for silliness as well. The element of ice cream could be suggested at some point for all I know, and I would take it to the logical conclusion - ice cream is fine, but if it has any addditives it fails the roll. Sprinkles are an automatic failure, because gosh darnit you do not put stuff on good icecream!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T06:49:35-08:00","id":838024,"title":"","content":"Pychic Energy would be a cool element. Subset of that could be Emotional Elementals, Rage Elemental,Terror Elemental, Humour Elemental, Lust Elemental.<br /> <br /> Bone would be cool and creepy, although it would only apply to dead bones, like wood is dead trees.<br /> <br /> X-Rays could be cool.<br /> <br /> Gravity Elemental, now that could be awesome.<br /> <br /> Magnetism Elemental.<br /> <br /> Glamour Elemental<br /> <br /> Emphereal Elemental (one made out of the stuff ghosts and spirits are.)<br /> <br /> Pot Elemental, just don't mix with a fire elemental unless you want everyone to get stoned.<br /> <br /> Slime Elemental<br /> <br /> Mana Elemental<br /> <br /> Dragon's Scales Elemental<br /> <br /> An Antimatter Elemental<br /> <br /> A Dark Matter/Energy Elemental<br /> <br /> A Plasma Elemental<br /> <br /> Picture a Darkling with Control Elements: Gravity, he or she basicly summoned a blackhole.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 02-27-2016, 09:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T06:55:53-08:00","id":838030,"title":"","content":"A Darkling with control elements light,could summon light and surround it with darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T07:25:37-08:00","id":838043,"title":"","content":"Then how come you had to cast magic missile?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T07:26:10-08:00","id":838044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/837889-2e-elements-contracts-what-can-changelings-wield?p=837978#post837978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When these threads come up, I never quite fail to recall that line from SpellCrash where a character complains that she wasn't allowed to pick &quot;sex&quot; as her element.</div> </div> </div> </div>You'll be thankful you can't when you think about Armor of the Elements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T08:06:39-08:00","id":838059,"title":"","content":"Don't forget the element of surprise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T08:38:10-08:00","id":838065,"title":"","content":"Hmm...<br /> <br /> Flour - Elemental Armor doubles as a very spooky ghost disguise<br /> Flower - not to be confused with the above<br /> Itching - &quot;not sure what this stuff is, exactly, but it's <i>really</i> itchy&quot;<br /> Oil - doesn't get along with water elementals<br /> Paper - because paper cuts are just the worst<br /> Pine - truly the most pleasant-smelling of elements<br /> Pollen - a truly deadly weapon, assuming your foe is allergic","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T10:21:25-08:00","id":838127,"title":"","content":"For Ziggy's contracts, I also considered using gravity for Cloak of Elements. Given that Ziggy builds on lunar associations, and his escape involved using the land tides created by an enormous Arcadian moon, I think it's appropriate. The defensive boost comes from deflecting blows, and the offensive damage comes from the gravity hurling opponents to the ground, into obstacles, or hurling obstacles into opponents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T11:50:14-08:00","id":838152,"title":"","content":"An idea this inspired within me, Darkling Telluric, who is black as the void, but with a fiery aura like the event horizon of a blackhole, whose mien exerts a sublte gravitational pull.<br /> <br /> This changeling would have Lethal Mien, his fists can boost their gravitational pull when they hit something and they're event horizan burns.<br /> <br /> This Changeling can summon gravitational elements via control element: gravity and cloak it in darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T15:06:05-08:00","id":838239,"title":"","content":"Dust may be another element that could be manipulated, or smoke - after all, entropy is a real thing, and smoke and dust when breathed in or even on one's eyes are quite hard to deal with. For that reason, too, they'd be great to have an inherent defense against.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T18:31:56-08:00","id":838336,"title":"","content":"Other possibly types of Elements.<br /> <br /> Ectoplasm<br /> <br /> Rubber<br /> <br /> Graphite<br /> <br /> Vitae<br /> <br /> Essence<br /> <br /> Pyros<br /> <br /> Body Fluids<br /> <br /> This list is good for Phantom Glory: Elemental edition. That is to say for those with the Phantom Glory contract and elemental effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T18:34:36-08:00","id":838339,"title":"","content":"I would personally scratch Vitae and Essence from the list, and I would <i>definitely</i> never include Pyros on there, if for no other reason than I just can't see fairies successfully negotiating a contract with it(though as a Chronicle focus, that could be interesting).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T00:43:26-08:00","id":838530,"title":"","content":"I love how the examples people are making are so grandiose.<br /> <br /> some other, lesser, element ideas are<br /> <br /> -vapour <br /> <br /> -smoke<br /> <br /> -glass<br /> <br /> -sand<br /> <br /> -plastic<br /> <br /> -rubber<br /> <br /> -wool<br /> <br /> -paper","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1377-wrequis","name":"Wrequis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T05:10:23-08:00","id":838583,"title":"","content":"Actually for Vitae I was thinking that making the contract via the strix could be interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T06:35:03-08:00","id":838614,"title":"","content":"A fellow player suggested &quot;hair&quot; as an element for a game. I thought it sounded fascinating. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T09:00:12-08:00","id":839223,"title":"","content":"I mean, based on the examples given, I'd personally apply the same rules to current-elemental-contracts as to the old ones. Namely, it must be a homogeneous, non-conceptual, mass noun. So bone, hair, mayonnaise, plasma, fabric, those are fine. I wouldn't use anything magic (Vitae, Pyros, etc), and I'd limit how broad or specific it was (matter is too broad; chocolate ice cream is too specific). But that's just me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T09:04:23-08:00","id":839229,"title":"","content":"I haven't heard anything to indicate that the nature of the elements has changed. So long as it's a conceivable base matter/energy for the Arcadian Realm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T09:55:46-08:00","id":839264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/837889-2e-elements-contracts-what-can-changelings-wield?p=839229#post839229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So long as it's a conceivable base matter/energy for the Arcadian Realm.</div> </div> </div> </div>For some reason I'm reminded of this quote from Angel:<br /> <br /> &quot;I walked worlds of smoke and half-truths, intangible. Worlds of torment and of unnamable beauty. Opaline towers as high as small moons. Glaciers that rippled with insensate lust. And one world with nothing but shrimp. I tired of that one quickly.&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T03:56:50-08:00","id":840536,"title":"","content":"Crayons, weed, bacon, explosions, America","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Meow! Meow meow meow. Purrrrrr.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11326-misterscruffles","name":"Misterscruffles","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T06:00:47-08:00","id":840585,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure I want to know what an America Elemental looks like. I keep picturing a cross between Uncle Sam and Wonder Women, and beard really doesn't match the tiara.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T10:04:58-08:00","id":840740,"title":"","content":"Paper is an extremely viable element. Just ask Yomiko Readman. Light as an element? Beware my power.<br /> <br /> But no sharks. Sharks are not an element, I don't care what SyFy's management thinks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T11:19:14-08:00","id":840792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/837889-2e-elements-contracts-what-can-changelings-wield?p=840585#post840585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure I want to know what an America Elemental looks like. I keep picturing a cross between Uncle Sam and Wonder Women, and beard really doesn't match the tiara.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eagles shooting rifles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T11:23:29-08:00","id":840793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/837889-2e-elements-contracts-what-can-changelings-wield?p=840792#post840792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eagles shooting rifles.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say feathers made out of bombs, nowadays.<br /> <br /> While guzzling oil and eating a steak.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T11:34:44-08:00","id":840800,"title":"","content":"Basically slap Deadpoool in a Captain America suit and then turn him into a were-eagle, that's an American Elemental. God Bless and everything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T11:56:42-08:00","id":840812,"title":"","content":"My personal restriction is that it can be anything that's present in reality and somehow observable with the naked eye. So no invisible forces like sound and magnetism, sorry. That said, I've allowed elementalists to control sound through Element (wind), including the point of creating full symphonies with the right powers. Magnetism I flat out banned, due to the fact that only iron-derived substances are magnetic in any way, and I don't like the idea of any Contract working on iron. Same reason I don't allow Element (blood). There's actually a bit of an odd relationship with vampires in my setting because of the iron element within blood having an unpredictable effect on fae magic. <br /> <br /> Some interesting elements I've used - Food (edible carbon-based non-living material), bone, silk (spiders!), feathers, polution and poison, radioactive isotopes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T12:20:08-08:00","id":840833,"title":"","content":"My rule of thumb is that anything that is thematically an element is an element. Arcadia does not give a flying carp about the chemical composition of something, it cares about themes and cultural significance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T12:27:32-08:00","id":840839,"title":"","content":"So, Ranch Dressing is now allowed, for instance? As well as Lame, and Bears?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 03-02-2016, 03:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T12:29:33-08:00","id":840841,"title":"","content":"So, as a serious question, what games are y'all playing where Ranch Dressing can be considered a fundamental element of your Keeper's Domain?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T12:30:53-08:00","id":840843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/837889-2e-elements-contracts-what-can-changelings-wield?p=840841#post840841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, as a serious question, what games are y'all playing where Ranch Dressing can be considered a fundamental element of your Keeper's Domain?</div> </div> </div> </div>'Twas a reference to <a href=\"http://oots.wikia.com/wiki/Semi-Elemental_Plane_of_Ranch_Dressing\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T12:49:59-08:00","id":840857,"title":"","content":"I am amused.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T13:22:46-08:00","id":840881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/837889-2e-elements-contracts-what-can-changelings-wield?p=840841#post840841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, as a serious question, what games are y'all playing where Ranch Dressing can be considered a fundamental element of your Keeper's Domain?</div> </div> </div> </div>This had me laughing for quite a while, since I could see this being a genuine Domain from a particularly strange Keeper.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/837889-2e-elements-contracts-what-can-changelings-wield?p=840812#post840812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My personal restriction is that it can be anything that's present in reality and somehow observable with the naked eye. So no invisible forces like sound and magnetism, sorry. That said, I've allowed elementalists to control sound through Element (wind), including the point of creating full symphonies with the right powers. Magnetism I flat out banned, due to the fact that only iron-derived substances are magnetic in any way, and I don't like the idea of any Contract working on iron. Same reason I don't allow Element (blood). There's actually a bit of an odd relationship with vampires in my setting because of the iron element within blood having an unpredictable effect on fae magic.<br /> <br /> Some interesting elements I've used - Food (edible carbon-based non-living material), bone, silk (spiders!), feathers, polution and poison, radioactive isotopes.</div> </div> </div> </div>The reason I pondered on Sound was because I'd thought of a Minstrel/Metalskin Changeling, who would sing/scream into her hands to produce an appropriate source for her contract to work from, and also giving her a thematic element to work with (it'd also make for a killer Black Canary cosplay - complete with Canary Cry). Still, I appreciate where you're coming from, particularly with magnetism...although I have to wonder how radioactive isotopes, being something that's far too small to see, could be a viable and wieldable thing (not to mention balanced, given how radiation tends to cause things to die). Wind being used to make sound is a nice alternative, however - perhaps it could be the power of Breath?<br /> <br /> Edit: I should note I don't know the particulars of radioactive isotopes, so it may not be that unfeasible. Just throwing in my two cents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","user":"Taidragon","date":". 03-02-2016, 07:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T16:16:40-08:00","id":840973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/837889-2e-elements-contracts-what-can-changelings-wield?p=840881#post840881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The reason I pondered on Sound was because I'd thought of a Minstrel/Metalskin Changeling, who would sing/scream into her hands to produce an appropriate source for her contract to work from, and also giving her a thematic element to work with (it'd also make for a killer Black Canary cosplay - complete with Canary Cry). Still, I appreciate where you're coming from, particularly with magnetism...although I have to wonder how radioactive isotopes, being something that's far too small to see, could be a viable and wieldable thing (not to mention balanced, given how radiation tends to cause things to die). Wind being used to make sound is a nice alternative, however - perhaps it could be the power of Breath?</div> </div> </div> </div> Oh, I totally understand where the whole sound thing is coming from. I had a player like that as well, when 1e came out. My conclusion was that I just don't like how sound worked with the Elemental Contracts, let alone Communion. Sure, Cloak would work, but &quot;calling&quot; it? Becoming it? That's why I put the restrictions I did in place. Because it should make solid literary sense, and it didn't quite. And we developed Sound through different other powers instead. <br /> <br /> As for radioactive isotopes? I might have used the wrong word. I was thinking of the rods in nuclear plants, which is clearly visible and glowing due to the isotopes. I figure at this point, radioactive glow is similar enough to the element of light, that I could get behind that. As for how to balance it? I simply ran it as a poison. Poison is pretty potent as it is.<br /> <br /> When it comes to powers, I tend to go for as broad a definition as possible. &quot;Wind&quot; would include air of all sorts, breath, sound and potentially some cloud magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T17:50:39-08:00","id":841033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/837889-2e-elements-contracts-what-can-changelings-wield?p=840973#post840973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Oh, I totally understand where the whole sound thing is coming from. I had a player like that as well, when 1e came out. My conclusion was that I just don't like how sound worked with the Elemental Contracts, let alone Communion. Sure, Cloak would work, but &quot;calling&quot; it? Becoming it? That's why I put the restrictions I did in place. Because it should make solid literary sense, and it didn't quite. And we developed Sound through different other powers instead.<br /> <br /> As for radioactive isotopes? I might have used the wrong word. I was thinking of the rods in nuclear plants, which is clearly visible and glowing due to the isotopes. I figure at this point, radioactive glow is similar enough to the element of light, that I could get behind that. As for how to balance it? I simply ran it as a poison. Poison is pretty potent as it is.<br /> <br /> When it comes to powers, I tend to go for as broad a definition as possible. &quot;Wind&quot; would include air of all sorts, breath, sound and potentially some cloud magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, now I understand. I thought you meant radiation in its minutia, the atoms and neutrons and so forth, rather than radioactive objects. That makes complete sense now, and though I probably wouldn't be too fond of running radiation as a mere poison, it works well enough that I could get behind it (if nothing else, it makes walking through nuclear fallout more bearable). Heck, with that kind of reasoning you could probably run a game of Fallout: Changeling edition and come away with some interesting elements.<br /> <br /> I never got to play Changeling 1E, since the GM found his muse was leaning far more towards Geist and we transitioned to that instead. However, given what I've read of 2E (and admittedly 1E) my understanding of &quot;Element&quot; is a force in the world that exists or could exist naturally but doesn't have a great deal of life behind it. They are forces that are about the world and though they can be called upon for assistance, that same wielding is used as a defense as well. Ergo, while I wouldn't consider Animals wouldn't to be an element, things like Dust, Water, Sound, Light, Stone and even something as insubstantial as Shadow would be viable, as they are primal forces to be wielded and protected against; some of them would likely come up more than others (I can't think of a mundane source of &quot;darkness&quot; that a Cloak could provide immunity to) but in this crazy World of Darkness, there's likely some magical source that any of these would be handy against.<br /> <br /> I see what you mean regarding the powers, as you don't want to make players investing in Cloak of Elements (Wind), only to find that they are faced with a tornado which goes above a mere &quot;wind&quot;. However, by that same logic I feel that some restraint should be given to what these powers would affect. If a Changeling had Cloak of Elements (Wind) and they stood in a gale, they would probably come out of it without any damage to their hearing, even if a normal person may have a slight ringing in their ears; however, if that same Changeling were to use that Cloak of Elements (Wind) behind a jetliner while it was taking off, they wouldn't be knocked down by the air currents the engines generate, but the sound and heat coming from them wouldn't be protected against, as it's not the wind ripping by them that is causing the damage but something made by the engines themselves. Likewise, having a Cloak of Elements (Sound) would protect the Changeling from going deaf in a similar situation or being thrown around by a sonic wave, but they'd be thrown quite a ways by air currents.<br /> <br /> As of now, I've not seen a contract that allows a Changeling to become an element, which may become problematic with certain elements such as, well, Sound, but in that case I'd apply comic book logic to it; if it doesn't make the user invisible, it should make them visible but patterned after their element. In the case of sound, lots of ripples, transparent, echoey when speaking, all that jazz (if you'll pardon the pun). Communion I can see working, given Elements called upon - after all, a spirit of Sound would know what someone was saying, and how loud or quiet their steps were, but if it were to be asked what color something was or a design on something they carried, they'd be out of luck, since such things don't leave anything to sound, not even to a stretch like echolocaton. I do appreciate why you put the restriction in place though, and I applaud your way of working around the issue. It hope you guys had a good time in that session.<br /> <br /> Apologies for the rambliness of this post. :-p","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T06:29:06-08:00","id":841266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/837889-2e-elements-contracts-what-can-changelings-wield?p=841033#post841033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> (I can't think of a mundane source of &quot;darkness&quot; that a Cloak could provide immunity to)</div> </div> </div> </div> In 1e, I ran that as protection from blindness. As in, you could always see in the darkest of nights without a light source. Gouging out eyes still worked.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I see what you mean regarding the powers, as you don't want to make players investing in Cloak of Elements (Wind), only to find that they are faced with a tornado which goes above a mere &quot;wind&quot;. However, by that same logic I feel that some restraint should be given to what these powers would affect. If a Changeling had Cloak of Elements (Wind) and they stood in a gale, they would probably come out of it without any damage to their hearing, even if a normal person may have a slight ringing in their ears; however, if that same Changeling were to use that Cloak of Elements (Wind) behind a jetliner while it was taking off, they wouldn't be knocked down by the air currents the engines generate, but the sound and heat coming from them wouldn't be protected against, as it's not the wind ripping by them that is causing the damage but something made by the engines themselves. Likewise, having a Cloak of Elements (Sound) would protect the Changeling from going deaf in a similar situation or being thrown around by a sonic wave, but they'd be thrown quite a ways by air currents. </div> </div> </div> See, I would allow the Wind Elementalist to be protected against the sound and being blown away by wind currents from a jet engine. In 1e, the Cloak had a specific catch that changelings could still be hurt by the elements if it was used as a weapon. A jet engine isn't a weapon, but a concussive grenade is. 2e works differently - the Cloak of the Elements flat out would protect you against any instances of &quot;wind&quot; damage so long as its not magical. Of course, we get into some question about Task Force Valkyrie and their pseudo-scientific equipment being potentially magical, but that's another matter.<br /> <br /> Heat would still be a problem, unless we start talking Element (fire).<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As of now, I've not seen a contract that allows a Changeling to become an element, </div> </div> </div> Actually, they hid it as the Elemental subset of Phantom Glory - this power is a combination of Elements 5 and Separation 5 from the old game. Its not as much of an issue with the new game, since you can opt out of it in such a niche spot, but it felt strained in the old one where it was a capstone of a power. Not to mention that you don't have to &quot;call&quot; the element, or shape it. Sound does fit nicer in the new power set than the old one.<br /> <br /> Where Sound in the new one runs into issues is using Control Elements (ooo). You inflict one of five Environmental Tilts - Blizzard, Earthquake, Flooded, Heavy Winds or Inferno (and Blinded with the Darkling option for Shadow / Light used alongside other elements). I'm personally looking at Heavy Winds and wondering if its appropriate? To quote from Beast pdf on Heavy Winds-<br /> <br /> &quot;Heavy winds are loud, so characters suffer a \u22123 modifier to aural Perception rolls. Also the wind inflicts a penalty to all Physical rolls when out in the winds \u2014 including Drive rolls. Grade the wind from one to five \u2014 one is tropical storm level (around 40 MPH), three is hurricane level (around 80 MPH), and five is tornado level (150+ MPH). This is the penalty applied to Physical dice rolls. Characters outside in the maelstrom take damage from flying debris, taking bashing damage each turn equal to the wind\u2019s rating. Characters can make a reflexive Dexterity + Athletics roll to avoid damage.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Perception roll check makes sense, but I'd almost want to go for Deafen instead. The damage and penalty also makes sense, kind of. Its not how I'd like to see it modeled, but its workable, I suppose. Though, I think I'd rather use Murkblur - that Blinds, Deafens, and can Stun and send someone Insensate.<br /> <br /> -------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> EDIT - the full list of Environmental Tilts that I see across all games are Ice, Heavy Winds, Heavy Rains, Flooded, Extreme Heat, Extreme Cold, Earthquake, Drowning, Blizard, and Avalanch. I'll add in Blind, Deafen, and Poisoned/Sick since they're the form of some fairly popular elements. <br /> <br /> Oddly enough, there's no option for poison in Contracts, though Brewer and Venombite kiths have some. Ice shows up in Flickering Hours, and we talked about Murkblur already, which is possibly appropriate for sound deafening/disorienting people. Extreme Heat/Cold is part of Night's Subtle Distractions. <br /> <br /> I see nothing for Avalanch, Drowning or Heavy Rains, which is understandable. Avalanches are hard to pull off in most cities, Drowning really shoudl be personal as the result of Flooded, and Heavy Rains mostly served to create the Flooded, Heavy Winds, and Extreme Cold Tilts. <br /> <br /> Most other Elemental themed abilities in the list tended to be plant based or artifice based (woodblood/manikin). Even making a fetch-like being!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 03-03-2016, 10:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T09:14:04-08:00","id":841340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/837889-2e-elements-contracts-what-can-changelings-wield?p=840800#post840800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically slap Deadpoool in a Captain America suit and then turn him into a were-eagle, that's an American Elemental. God Bless and everything.</div> </div> </div> </div> And then have him run for President.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T09:22:17-08:00","id":841343,"title":"","content":"Light is actually a pretty cool element because you burn things as if its a laser, power solar cells, create holograms by bending light, or rainbow, light up an area, ect...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T09:23:25-08:00","id":841345,"title":"","content":"The Doctor from Voyager would be a light element.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T11:00:14-08:00","id":841393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/837889-2e-elements-contracts-what-can-changelings-wield?p=841340#post841340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And then have him run for President.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Metal_Wolf_Chaos\" target=\"_blank\">Michael Wilson</a>, is that you?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T01:49:54-08:00","id":841788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/837889-2e-elements-contracts-what-can-changelings-wield?p=840812#post840812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Magnetism I flat out banned, due to the fact that only iron-derived substances are magnetic in any way, and I don't like the idea of any Contract working on iron.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is flat out not true, though. <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Lt4P6ctf06Q\" target=\"_blank\">oxygen is magnetic, for instance</a>. And most of the transition metals (D/F blocks) are capable of being diamagnetic or paramagnetic.<br /> <br /> This is your daily science interruption. Blame the fact that I have been doing Chemistry tutorials all week. :P<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/837889-2e-elements-contracts-what-can-changelings-wield?p=841345#post841345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Doctor from Voyager would be a light element.</div> </div> </div> </div>He'd make a good Light Elemental, too. Actually, the Doctor is great. He'd be a fun character achetype to play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T02:48:13-08:00","id":841795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/837889-2e-elements-contracts-what-can-changelings-wield?p=841343#post841343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Light is actually a pretty cool element because you burn things as if its a laser, power solar cells, create holograms by bending light, or rainbow, light up an area, ect...</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like using Control Elements: Light to create holograms is a bit much... ... ... though now I wonder if Control Elements: Color would be a thing<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T04:54:56-08:00","id":841826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/837889-2e-elements-contracts-what-can-changelings-wield?p=841788#post841788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is flat out not true, though. <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Lt4P6ctf06Q\" target=\"_blank\">oxygen is magnetic, for instance</a>. And most of the transition metals (D/F blocks) are capable of being diamagnetic or paramagnetic.<br /> <br /> This is your daily science interruption. Blame the fact that I have been doing Chemistry tutorials all week. :P</div> </div> </div> </div> Huh. Good to know. I probably still would say no affecting Iron through magnetism, though. Of course, I don't let Artifice work on iron either. So, that may just be my house rules with making iron more significant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T10:33:18-08:00","id":841980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/837889-2e-elements-contracts-what-can-changelings-wield?p=841795#post841795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel like using Control Elements: Light to create holograms is a bit much... ... ... though now I wonder if Control Elements: Color would be a thing</div> </div> </div> </div> Colours ARE light at different wavelengths.<br /> <br /> col\u00b7or<br /> <br /> \u02c8k\u0259l\u0259r/<br /> <br /> noun<br /> <br /> noun: colour<br /> <br /> 1.<br /> <br /> the property possessed by an object of producing different sensations on the eye as a result of the way the object reflects or emits light.<br /> <br /> &quot;the lights flickered and changed color&quot;<br /> <br /> synonyms:hue, shade, tint, tone, coloration<br /> <br /> &quot;the lights changed color&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T14:28:59-08:00","id":842159,"title":"","content":"Light elementals producing holograms is a perfectly sensible thing to do, I'd say. But then, I'm sure if I ever played one such character with high science they'd use the photoelectric effect to generate electricity too.<br /> <br /> Heh. That's an idea. Solar Panel Tech is really a Changeling with Elements: Light<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/837889-2e-elements-contracts-what-can-changelings-wield?p=841826#post841826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Huh. Good to know. I probably still would say no affecting Iron through magnetism, though. Of course, I don't let Artifice work on iron either. So, that may just be my house rules with making iron more significant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, that makes perfect sense. Iron is iron and it's Changeling. You can work around it pretty easily though, magnetism is everywhere too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T16:29:48-08:00","id":842226,"title":"","content":"Would it make sense to change Control Elements to give you an effective Influence (Elements) rating?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Meow! Meow meow meow. Purrrrrr.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11326-misterscruffles","name":"Misterscruffles","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T17:17:04-08:00","id":842259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/837889-2e-elements-contracts-what-can-changelings-wield?p=841266#post841266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> In 1e, I ran that as protection from blindness. As in, you could always see in the darkest of nights without a light source. Gouging out eyes still worked.<br /> <br /> See, I would allow the Wind Elementalist to be protected against the sound and being blown away by wind currents from a jet engine. In 1e, the Cloak had a specific catch that changelings could still be hurt by the elements if it was used as a weapon. A jet engine isn't a weapon, but a concussive grenade is. 2e works differently - the Cloak of the Elements flat out would protect you against any instances of &quot;wind&quot; damage so long as its not magical. Of course, we get into some question about Task Force Valkyrie and their pseudo-scientific equipment being potentially magical, but that's another matter.<br /> <br /> Heat would still be a problem, unless we start talking Element (fire).</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair point with the Cloak of Elements (Shadows); I suppose Cloak of Elements (Light) would provide a similar defense, albeit one that prevented damage from looking into light sources (like the sun). As for the jet engine scenario, I suppose it's simply a difference in our preferences.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/837889-2e-elements-contracts-what-can-changelings-wield?p=841266#post841266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Actually, they hid it as the Elemental subset of Phantom Glory - this power is a combination of Elements 5 and Separation 5 from the old game. Its not as much of an issue with the new game, since you can opt out of it in such a niche spot, but it felt strained in the old one where it was a capstone of a power. Not to mention that you don't have to &quot;call&quot; the element, or shape it. Sound does fit nicer in the new power set than the old one.<br /> <br /> Where Sound in the new one runs into issues is using Control Elements (ooo). You inflict one of five Environmental Tilts - Blizzard, Earthquake, Flooded, Heavy Winds or Inferno (and Blinded with the Darkling option for Shadow / Light used alongside other elements). I'm personally looking at Heavy Winds and wondering if its appropriate? To quote from Beast pdf on Heavy Winds-<br /> <br /> &quot;Heavy winds are loud, so characters suffer a \u22123 modifier to aural Perception rolls. Also the wind inflicts a penalty to all Physical rolls when out in the winds \u2014 including Drive rolls. Grade the wind from one to five \u2014 one is tropical storm level (around 40 MPH), three is hurricane level (around 80 MPH), and five is tornado level (150+ MPH). This is the penalty applied to Physical dice rolls. Characters outside in the maelstrom take damage from flying debris, taking bashing damage each turn equal to the wind\u2019s rating. Characters can make a reflexive Dexterity + Athletics roll to avoid damage.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Perception roll check makes sense, but I'd almost want to go for Deafen instead. The damage and penalty also makes sense, kind of. Its not how I'd like to see it modeled, but its workable, I suppose.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh, I hadn't noticed that until you pointed it out since I've been more focused on the lower level contracts. I can see where that would cause problems without the GM doing some homebrewing. It's nice that the new setup has more fluidity to it.<br /> <br /> Tilt-wise, I can see where you're coming from. Given how shockwaves can knock things down and cause quite a bit of damage, sound being a form of pressure, I would say that Heavy Winds would be appropriate. That said, if the Changeling does it a certain way they may go for something akin to the Earthquake tilt, if they channel the shockwave through the ground, or the Avalanche tilt if in an appropriate area. Deafen would work well too, though if it isn't a major tilt you could make a lesser version of the elemental ones to go with it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/837889-2e-elements-contracts-what-can-changelings-wield?p=842159#post842159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Light elementals producing holograms is a perfectly sensible thing to do, I'd say. But then, I'm sure if I ever played one such character with high science they'd use the photoelectric effect to generate electricity too.<br /> <br /> Heh. That's an idea. Solar Panel Tech is really a Changeling with Elements: Light</div> </div> </div> </div>And now you make me want to host a space-based Changeling 2E game, possibly where a freehold takes place in a space station. Each Changeling has their role to play, such as Changelings with Control Elements (Light) makes sure the solar panels keep generating power evenly, whereas various plant based Changelings deal with creating foodstuffs so everyone survives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}